    <!-- SECTION 7: SOC FABRICS, INTERCONNECTS & CLUSTERS (SOC & MULTI-CORE BRIDGE) -->
    <!-- ============================================================ -->
    <section id="soc-interconnects" class="fund-section-card">
      <div class="fund-header">
        <span class="fund-num">07</span>
        <div>
          <a href="/soc-multicore/" style="text-decoration: none;"><span class="badge badge-accent">SOC &amp; MULTI-CORE &bull; MANYCORE SYSTEMS &rarr;</span></a>
          <h2 class="fund-title">SoC Interconnect Fabrics &amp; Multi-Core Clusters</h2>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="fund-lead">
        A processor core in isolation cannot run an application without peripherals, memory controllers, and interconnect fabrics. <strong>System-on-Chip (SoC)</strong> architecture integrates dozens to hundreds of cores with coherent crossbars, Direct Memory Access (DMA) engines, and hardware synchronization units.
      </p>

      <!-- Top-Down Progression: Interconnects & Manycore Scaling -->
      <div class="concept-stream">
        <!-- 7.1 INTERCONNECT TOPOLOGIES -->
        <div class="concept-step-card">
          <div class="step-card-header">
            <span class="step-tag">7.1 INTERCONNECT EVOLUTION</span>
            <h3 class="step-card-title">Interconnect Topologies: Bus vs. Crossbar vs. 2D Mesh NoC</h3>
          </div>
          <p>
            How multiple cores communicate with multi-banked L2 memory:
          </p>
          <ul class="concept-list">
            <li><strong>Shared Bus (Wishbone / APB / OBI):</strong> Single shared communication backbone arbitrated by a central mux. Only one master transmits per cycle, saturating past 2 to 4 cores (e.g., <code>PULPissimo</code>, <code>CROC</code>, <code>OpenTitan</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>Full &amp; Logarithmic Crossbar (AXI4 / TileLink / TCDM):</strong> Parallel switch fabric allowing <em>M</em> masters to access <em>N</em> independent memory banks concurrently without blocking (e.g., <code>Cheshire</code>, <code>Snitch Cluster</code>, and 256-core logarithmic TCDM in <code>MemPool</code>).</li>
            <li><strong>2D Mesh Network-on-Chip (P-Mesh / FlooNoC):</strong> Packet-switched tiled router fabric scaling from 16 to 432+ cores via dimension-ordered X-Y routing hops (e.g., <code>OpenPiton</code>, <code>Picobello</code>, <code>Occamy</code>).</li>
          </ul>

