          <p>
            Overcoming manycore software bottlenecks:
          </p>
          <ul class="concept-list">
            <li><strong>Autonomous DMA:</strong> Direct Memory Access engines stream gigabytes of matrix tiles from external DRAM into local tightly-coupled SRAM buffers without halting the CPU.</li>
            <li><strong>The Manycore Spinlock Wall:</strong> When 256 cores wait for each other using software spinlocks (atomic memory operations), the crossbar congests. Manycore clusters (like <code>Snitch</code>) integrate dedicated <strong>hardware barrier wires</strong> to synchronize 256 cores in a single clock cycle!</li>
          </ul>

